import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"ADR-0032 Item 6: Proof Erasure at Runtime","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"handl/project/tasks/adr0032-proof-erasure.md","filePath":"vendored/handl/project/tasks/adr0032-proof-erasure.md"}`),a={name:`handl/project/tasks/adr0032-proof-erasure.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="adr-0032-item-6-proof-erasure-at-runtime" tabindex="-1">ADR-0032 Item 6: Proof Erasure at Runtime <a class="header-anchor" href="#adr-0032-item-6-proof-erasure-at-runtime" aria-label="Permalink to “ADR-0032 Item 6: Proof Erasure at Runtime”">​</a></h1><h2 id="goal" tabindex="-1">Goal <a class="header-anchor" href="#goal" aria-label="Permalink to “Goal”">​</a></h2><p>Wire proof-term erasure into the <code>Runtime::run_checked</code> pipeline so that the typechecker can tell the runtime which AST nodes are proofs, and the runtime replaces those nodes with a cheap <code>erased</code>/<code>null</code> node before evaluation. This removes the runtime cost of carrying proof terms while keeping the static type-safety guarantees intact.</p><h2 id="status" tabindex="-1">Status <a class="header-anchor" href="#status" aria-label="Permalink to “Status”">​</a></h2><p>in progress</p><h2 id="subtasks" tabindex="-1">Subtasks <a class="header-anchor" href="#subtasks" aria-label="Permalink to “Subtasks”">​</a></h2><h3 id="_1-add-the-erased-ast-node-and-eval-scheme" tabindex="-1">1. Add the <code>erased</code> AST node and eval scheme <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-add-the-erased-ast-node-and-eval-scheme" aria-label="Permalink to “1. Add the erased AST node and eval scheme”">​</a></h3><p>Status: <strong>done</strong></p><ul><li>Add an <code>ast.erased</code> leaf shape to <code>crates/handl-kit-data-canonical/data/ast.yaml</code> (no children, empty/null payload).</li><li>Add an <code>eval.erased</code> scheme to <code>crates/handl-kit-data-canonical/data/eval.yaml</code> that evaluates to <code>null</code> (e.g. <code>!Arr op: const</code> with no literal, so the existing tree-walk <code>const</code> native op returns <code>Value::Null</code>).</li><li>Add a unit or integration test verifying that an AST containing an <code>erased</code> node evaluates to <code>Value::Null</code>. <ul><li>Candidate locations: <code>crates/plugin-engine-exec-tree-walk/src/lib.rs</code> tests (native <code>const</code> tests already exist around line 3942), <code>crates/handl-runtime/src/lib.rs</code> tests, or a new <code>crates/handl-runtime/tests/proof_erasure.rs</code>.</li></ul></li></ul><p>Files expected to change:</p><ul><li><code>crates/handl-kit-data-canonical/data/ast.yaml</code></li><li><code>crates/handl-kit-data-canonical/data/eval.yaml</code></li><li><code>crates/handl-runtime/src/lib.rs</code> or <code>crates/handl-runtime/tests/proof_erasure.rs</code> (or <code>crates/plugin-engine-exec-tree-walk/src/lib.rs</code>)</li></ul><p>Verification:</p><ul><li><code>cargo test -p handl-plugin-engine-exec-tree-walk</code></li><li><code>cargo test -p handl-runtime</code></li></ul><p>Result (completed):</p><ul><li><code>ast.erased</code> shape appended to <code>data/ast.yaml</code> (no children, <code>payload_schema: {type: &quot;null&quot;}</code>).</li><li><code>eval.erased</code> scheme appended to <code>data/eval.yaml</code> (<code>!Arr op: const</code>, <code>args: []</code>, <code>source: Native</code>, no <code>lit</code> → returns <code>Value::Null</code>).</li><li>New integration test <code>crates/handl-runtime/tests/erased_node.rs</code>: <code>erased_node_evaluates_to_null</code> builds the canonical <code>Kit</code>, pushes an <code>erased</code> node with <code>null</code> payload, and asserts eval yields <code>null</code>.</li><li>Verification run: <ul><li><code>cargo test -p handl-runtime --test erased_node</code> — 1 passed.</li><li><code>cargo test -p handl-runtime</code> — all targets pass (120+ tests, 0 failed).</li><li><code>cargo test -p handl-plugin-engine-exec-tree-walk</code> — all pass (122 tests).</li><li><code>cargo test -p handl-kit-canonical</code> — 69 passed, <strong>2 pre-existing failures</strong> (<code>hello_greet_returns_canonical_greeting</code>, <code>hello_greet_bridge_escapes_special_chars</code>) that also fail with the new YAML entries reverted — unrelated dirty-tree state (<code>check_json_value: expected type is not a tagged type value</code> at <code>crates/kit-canonical/src/lib.rs:1031</code>).</li></ul></li></ul><h3 id="_2-expose-a-per-node-type-map-in-typecheckresult" tabindex="-1">2. Expose a per-node type map in <code>TypecheckResult</code> <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-expose-a-per-node-type-map-in-typecheckresult" aria-label="Permalink to “2. Expose a per-node type map in TypecheckResult”">​</a></h3><p>Status: <strong>done</strong></p><ul><li>Extend <code>TypecheckResult</code> in <code>crates/plugin-engine-typecheck/src/lib.rs</code> with a new field, e.g. <code>pub node_types: HashMap&lt;usize, Value&gt;</code> (keyed by <code>AstRef::index()</code>). Keep it backward-compatible by defaulting to an empty map.</li><li>In <code>crates/plugin-engine-typecheck-nbe/src/lib.rs</code>: <ul><li>Add <code>node_types: HashMap&lt;usize, Value&gt;</code> to <code>TypecheckContext</code> (around line 3991).</li><li>Record the synthesized/checked <code>Value</code> for every visited <code>AstRef</code> in <code>synth_node</code> (line 261) and <code>check_node</code> (line 285).</li><li>Populate <code>node_types</code> in <code>NbeTypecheckEngine::typecheck</code> (line 3939).</li></ul></li><li>Update the existing <code>TypecheckResult</code> constructors in test stubs: <code>crates/handl-runtime/src/lib.rs</code> (lines 1496 and 2229) and <code>crates/plugin-lib-lang-typecheck/src/tests.rs</code> (line 71).</li><li>Add a test in <code>crates/plugin-engine-typecheck-nbe/src/tests.rs</code> that typechecks a small expression and asserts <code>result.node_types</code> contains entries for the root and at least one child.</li></ul><p>Files expected to change:</p><ul><li><code>crates/plugin-engine-typecheck/src/lib.rs</code></li><li><code>crates/plugin-engine-typecheck-nbe/src/lib.rs</code></li><li><code>crates/plugin-engine-typecheck-nbe/src/tests.rs</code></li><li><code>crates/handl-runtime/src/lib.rs</code> (test stubs)</li><li><code>crates/plugin-lib-lang-typecheck/src/tests.rs</code></li></ul><p>Verification:</p><ul><li><code>cargo test -p handl-plugin-engine-typecheck-nbe</code></li><li><code>cargo test -p handl-runtime</code></li><li><code>cargo test -p handl-kit-canonical</code></li></ul><p>Result (completed):</p><ul><li><code>TypecheckResult</code> gained <code>pub node_types: HashMap&lt;usize, Value&gt;</code> (<code>crates/plugin-engine-typecheck/src/lib.rs</code>), keyed by <code>AstRef::index()</code>.</li><li><code>TypecheckContext</code> gained <code>node_types</code> (initialized in <code>TypecheckContext::new</code>); <code>synth_node</code> records the synthesized type and <code>check_node</code> records <code>expected</code> on the <code>check_scheme</code> branch and the synthesized <code>ty</code> on the synth-then-unify branch.</li><li><code>NbeTypecheckEngine::typecheck</code> returns <code>node_types: ctx.node_types</code>.</li><li>Stub constructors updated: <code>crates/handl-runtime/src/lib.rs</code> (two sites) and <code>crates/plugin-lib-lang-typecheck/src/tests.rs</code> — all use <code>node_types: Default::default()</code>.</li><li>New test <code>node_types_populated_after_typecheck</code> in <code>crates/plugin-engine-typecheck-nbe/src/tests.rs</code>: a <code>wrap{children:[0]}</code> AST over a <code>lit</code> child; asserts <code>node_types[1]</code> (root) and <code>node_types[0]</code> (child) both equal <code>type.number</code>.</li><li>Verification run: <ul><li><code>cargo test -p handl-plugin-engine-typecheck-nbe</code> — 251 + 46 tests, all pass (includes the new test).</li><li><code>cargo test -p handl-runtime</code> — all targets pass (100 lib + integration tests, 0 failed).</li><li><code>cargo test -p handl-plugin-engine-exec-tree-walk</code> — all pass.</li><li><code>cargo test -p handl-kit-canonical</code> — 69 passed, <strong>2 pre-existing failures</strong> (<code>hello_greet_returns_canonical_greeting</code>, <code>hello_greet_bridge_escapes_special_chars</code>, <code>check_json_value: expected type is not a tagged type value</code>) — same failures reported in subtask 1, unrelated dirty-tree state.</li></ul></li></ul><h3 id="_3-implement-erase-pass-and-wire-it-into-runtime-run-checked" tabindex="-1">3. Implement <code>erase_pass</code> and wire it into <code>Runtime::run_checked</code> <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-implement-erase-pass-and-wire-it-into-runtime-run-checked" aria-label="Permalink to “3. Implement erase_pass and wire it into Runtime::run_checked”">​</a></h3><p>Status: <strong>done</strong></p><ul><li>Created <code>crates/handl-runtime/src/erase_pass.rs</code>: <ul><li><code>apply_erase(lang, ast, node_types)</code> performs an in-place arena mutation.</li><li>Proof values are recognized by <code>__tag__</code> (<code>type.refl</code>, <code>type.is_evidence</code>, <code>type.empty</code>) and optional <code>__registry__ == &quot;handl.canonical&quot;</code>.</li><li>Matching nodes are rewritten to the <code>erased</code> node kind with a <code>null</code> payload. The <code>erased</code> kind is resolved from <code>lang.ast</code> by identity.</li></ul></li><li>Wired <code>erase_pass::apply_erase</code> into <code>Runtime::run_checked</code> after the <code>runtime_assert</code> pass and before <code>eval</code> (ADR-0032).</li><li>Added <code>pub mod erase_pass;</code> in <code>crates/handl-runtime/src/lib.rs</code>.</li><li>Added tests: <ul><li>Unit tests in <code>erase_pass.rs</code>: proof erasure, non-proof preservation, missing type info, and missing <code>__registry__</code>.</li><li>Integration test <code>crates/handl-runtime/tests/proof_erasure.rs</code>: <ul><li><code>run_checked_erases_proof_typed_root</code> — a <code>value(42)</code> node whose typechecker reports <code>type.refl</code> evaluates to <code>null</code>.</li><li><code>run_checked_preserves_computational_nodes</code> — a <code>value(42)</code> node whose type is <code>type.number</code> still evaluates to <code>42</code>.</li></ul></li></ul></li></ul><p>Files changed:</p><ul><li><code>crates/handl-runtime/src/erase_pass.rs</code> (new)</li><li><code>crates/handl-runtime/src/lib.rs</code></li><li><code>crates/handl-runtime/tests/proof_erasure.rs</code> (new)</li></ul><p>Verification (completed):</p><ul><li><code>cargo test -p handl-runtime --test proof_erasure</code> — 2 passed.</li><li><code>cargo test -p handl-runtime</code> — 130+ tests passed (including new <code>erase_pass</code> unit tests and the <code>erased_node</code> / <code>proof_erasure</code> integration tests).</li><li><code>cargo test -p handl-plugin-engine-typecheck-nbe</code> — 251 + 46 passed.</li><li><code>cargo test -p handl-plugin-engine-exec-tree-walk</code> — 116 + integration passed.</li><li><code>cargo test -p handl-plugin-engine-exec-bytecode</code> — 71 + 4 passed.</li><li><code>cargo test -p handl-plugin-engine-exec-cranelift --lib</code> — 79 passed.</li><li><code>cargo test -p handl-kit-canonical</code> — 69 passed, 2 pre-existing failures (<code>hello_greet_returns_canonical_greeting</code>, <code>hello_greet_bridge_escapes_special_chars</code>); unrelated to erasure.</li><li><code>cargo test -p handl-kit-data-canonical</code> — lib tests passed; integration test <code>full_language_parity::language_has_eval_schemes_for_all_major_node_kinds</code> fails on missing eval scheme for <code>let</code> (pre-existing, unrelated to erasure).</li></ul><h3 id="_4-end-to-end-verification-and-adr-status" tabindex="-1">4. End-to-end verification and ADR status <a class="header-anchor" href="#_4-end-to-end-verification-and-adr-status" aria-label="Permalink to “4. End-to-end verification and ADR status”">​</a></h3><p>Status: <strong>done</strong></p><ul><li>Ran the targeted crates (see subtask 3 verification) and confirmed that <code>data</code> desugaring, <code>match</code>, <code>runtime_assert</code>, and the new <code>erased</code> node work.</li><li>Updated <code>project/adrs/0032-types-as-values-remaining.md</code>: <ul><li>Marked item 6 (Proof erasure at runtime) as <strong>completed</strong>.</li><li>Added a note that built-in equality/membership proof erasure is in place and user-defined <code>data</code> proof-constructor erasure remains a follow-up.</li></ul></li><li>Left the optional <code>data</code> proof-constructor erasure in <code>crates/handl-runtime/src/desugar_pass.rs</code> as a future step; it requires surface syntax for marking constructors/types as <code>erased</code>/<code>proof</code>.</li></ul><p>Files changed:</p><ul><li><code>project/adrs/0032-types-as-values-remaining.md</code></li><li><code>project/tasks/adr0032-proof-erasure.md</code></li></ul><p>Verification (completed):</p><ul><li>Same targeted crate runs as subtask 3.</li><li><code>data</code> desugaring tests (<code>indexed_family_data</code>, <code>indexed_family_match</code>, <code>indexed_family_fin</code>) and <code>runtime_assert</code> tests remain green.</li></ul><h2 id="first-subtask-to-implement-next" tabindex="-1">First subtask to implement next <a class="header-anchor" href="#first-subtask-to-implement-next" aria-label="Permalink to “First subtask to implement next”">​</a></h2><p>All four subtasks are complete. The remaining follow-up is user-defined <code>data</code> proof-constructor erasure (marking a constructor or whole <code>data</code> declaration as <code>erased</code>/<code>proof</code> in surface syntax and dropping erased fields from generated constructors/recursors).</p><h2 id="related-files" tabindex="-1">Related files <a class="header-anchor" href="#related-files" aria-label="Permalink to “Related files”">​</a></h2><ul><li><code>project/adrs/0032-types-as-values-remaining.md</code></li><li><code>project/adrs/0082-inductive-types.md</code> (§5 — erasure deferred to this item)</li><li><code>project/adrs/0068-predicates-as-types.md</code> (Negative — no erasure yet)</li><li><code>crates/handl-runtime/src/lib.rs</code><ul><li><code>Runtime::typecheck</code> at line 827</li><li><code>Runtime::run_checked</code> at line 867</li></ul></li><li><code>crates/handl-runtime/src/desugar_pass.rs</code><ul><li><code>data</code> desugaring around line 1553</li></ul></li><li><code>crates/handl-runtime/src/runtime_assert_pass.rs</code><ul><li>template for in-place AST mutation</li></ul></li><li><code>crates/handl-kit-data-canonical/data/ast.yaml</code></li><li><code>crates/handl-kit-data-canonical/data/eval.yaml</code></li><li><code>crates/plugin-engine-typecheck/src/lib.rs</code><ul><li><code>TypecheckResult</code> at line 83</li></ul></li><li><code>crates/plugin-engine-typecheck-nbe/src/lib.rs</code><ul><li><code>synth_node</code> at line 261</li><li><code>check_node</code> at line 285</li><li><code>NbeTypecheckEngine::typecheck</code> at line 3927</li><li><code>TypecheckContext</code> at line 3991</li><li>equality/proof constructors (<code>construct_eq</code>, <code>check_refl</code>, <code>eq_reduce</code>) around line 2554</li><li>membership proof constructor (<code>check_membership</code>, <code>eval_membership</code>) around line 2753</li></ul></li><li><code>crates/plugin-engine-typecheck-nbe/src/tests.rs</code><ul><li><code>type_refl()</code> at line 7118</li><li><code>type_is_evidence()</code> at line 6727</li></ul></li><li><code>crates/handl-language/src/lib.rs</code><ul><li><code>Value</code> / <code>TAG_VALUE_KEY</code> / <code>REGISTRY_VALUE_KEY</code></li></ul></li><li><code>crates/plugin-engine-exec-tree-walk/src/lib.rs</code><ul><li><code>const</code> native op at line 1084</li></ul></li></ul><h2 id="notes-open-questions" tabindex="-1">Notes / open questions <a class="header-anchor" href="#notes-open-questions" aria-label="Permalink to “Notes / open questions”">​</a></h2><ul><li><p><strong>What counts as a proof term today?</strong></p><ul><li>Concrete singleton proof values are <code>type.refl</code> (equality proof) and <code>type.is_evidence</code> (membership proof), both minted by <code>TypeRegistry::construct</code> as tagged JSON objects with <code>__tag__</code> and <code>__registry__</code> keys.</li><li><code>type.empty</code> is the uninhabited proposition; if a node ever synthesizes it, it is also safe to erase.</li><li><code>type.eq</code> and <code>type.membership</code> are <em>proposition types</em> / type families, not proof values. Their inhabitants are <code>type.refl</code> and <code>type.is_evidence</code> respectively, so only those inhabitants should be erased.</li><li><code>data</code> constructors are currently ordinary tagged records; there is no <code>proof</code> or <code>erased</code> marker, so user-defined proof types are not yet recognized by the erasure pass.</li><li><code>Verdict::Proven</code> / <code>Verdict::Blocked</code> are compile-time outcomes of the predicate checker, not runtime values. They only control whether the <code>runtime_assert</code> pass runs.</li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Where should erasure run?</strong></p><ul><li>The chosen design is an <strong>AST pass between typecheck and eval</strong>.</li><li>The typechecker records per-node types and returns them in <code>TypecheckResult::node_types</code>.</li><li><code>Runtime::run_checked</code> calls <code>erase_pass::apply_erase</code> after the <code>runtime_assert</code> lowering and before <code>eval</code>.</li><li>Erasure is <strong>not</strong> done inside the typechecker (too engine-specific) and <strong>not</strong> as a runtime eval scheme (that would still build the proof value before discarding it, defeating the purpose).</li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Precondition / blocker:</strong><code>TypecheckResult</code> currently only returns the root type. Subtask 2 (per-node type map) is the main blocker for the full erase pass.</p></li><li><p><strong>Open question — ordering relative to <code>runtime_assert_pass</code>:</strong> Proposed order is <code>typecheck</code> → <code>runtime_assert_pass</code> → <code>erase_pass</code> → <code>eval</code>. This keeps blocked runtime checks intact and only nullifies nodes whose type is already a singleton proof. Revisit if any erased constructor is needed by a <code>runtime_assert</code> predicate.</p></li><li><p><strong>Open question — <code>data</code> proof constructors:</strong> Built-in equality/membership proofs are covered by the <code>type.refl</code> / <code>type.is_evidence</code> tags. User-defined <code>data</code> proof types (e.g. <code>data Eq(a, b) = Refl</code>) will need an additional desugaring signal, such as an <code>erased</code> field on <code>DataConstructor</code>, before the erase pass can handle them. This is tracked as the optional follow-up in Subtask 4.</p></li></ul>`,44)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};